624 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (At the heart of Neuralink's technology is a chip containing neuron-sized threads, which is surgically implanted into the brain. The tiny flexible threads fan out with minuscule electrodes which can monitor brain activity and stimulate neurons as needed. The chip then transmits this neural data via a wireless connection to an external device, which is typically operating on Bluetooth Protocol. The interface allows information to not only be read from the brain but also delivered into it, creating a symbiotic relationship between biological and digital intelligence. The science behind how these implants work is not different from how you would go about trying to measure the energy from an AA battery which is known as neuro electrophysiological recording. For example, when you move your arm to the right, certain sets of neurons are activated in a certain pattern. Listening to that activity and that pattern, you can predict very quickly which direction the arm is going to move. These are the neurons that are directly wired to your muscles.)
/E (At the heart of Neuralink's technology is a chip containing neuron-sized threads, which is surgically implanted into the brain. The tiny flexible threads fan out with minuscule electrodes which can monitor brain activity and stimulate neurons as needed. The chip then transmits this neural data via a wireless connection to an external device, which is typically operating on Bluetooth Protocol. The interface allows information to not only be read from the brain but also delivered into it, creating a symbiotic relationship between biological and digital intelligence. The science behind how these implants work is not different from how you would go about trying to measure the energy from an AA battery which is known as neuro electrophysiological recording. For example, when you move your arm to the right, certain sets of neurons are activated in a certain pattern. Listening to that activity and that pattern, you can predict very quickly which direction the arm is going to move. These are the neurons that are directly wired to your muscles.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
